  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mariammal vs The Designated Officer on 3 December, 2024 Author: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan Bench: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 03.12.2024 Coram The Honourable Mr. Justice G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P (MD).No.28855 of 2024 Mariammal ...Petition Vs. 1.The Designated Officer, Tamil Nadu Food Safety & Drug Administration Department, Collectorate Campus, Virudhunagar-626 002. 2.The Superintendent of Police, Virudhunagar District, Virudhunagar. 3.The Food Safety Officer, Sattur Municipality, Near Old Panchayat Office, Sattur, Virudhunagar District. 4.The Inspector of Police, Sattur Taluk Police Station, Sattur, Virudhunagar District. ...Responde Prayer: Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution o issue a Writ of Mandamus, to direct the respondents, particularly, the respondents 3 & 4 to forthwith remove the lock and seal imposed on the petitioner's teashop situated at No.6/32, West Street, Nadusurangudi, Sa Taluk, Virudhunagar District and permit the petitioner to resume her bus operations. https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 1/5 W.P Mariammal vs The Designated Officer on 3 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/102239154/ 1 For Petitioner : Mr.P.Saravanakumar For R1 to R3 : Mr.D.Gandhi Raj Special Government Ple For R4 : Mrs.M.Aasha Government Advocate (C Order",
    "facts": "In pursuant to the seizure of the Tobacco cigarettes, FIR has been registered in Cr.No.135 of 2024 for the offences under Section 123 of Bhartiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS), 2023 r/w Section 6(b) and 24(1) of Cigarettes and other Tobacco Products Acts 2003. On the information, the third respondent locked the premises for further proceeding. During the first time, the petitioner was imposed a fine and he has paid the same. Once again, the petitioner committed the very same offence and as such the petitioner's shop has been locked by the third respondent. Without completing the entire proceedings, the lock and seal of the petitioner's shop cannot be removed and the hence, the request made by the petitioner cannot be considered.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
